<title>USA: Florida regents put $13.15 million revs on notice.</title>
<headline>Florida regents put $13.15 million revs on notice.</headline>
<dateline>TALLAHASSEE, Fla 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Board of Regents will sell $13.15 million of revenue bonds by competitive bid with 20 hours notice, the state Division of Bond Finance said Monday.</p>
<p>The issue is designated Board of Regents Florida State University Housing Facility Revenue Bonds, Series 1996, and will have maturities out to 2026.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
